  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis afternoon a weak upper-level trough moves over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will bring showers and \nthunderstorms to Southwestern Montana this afternoon and evening. It \nwill warm up across the area with mostly dry weather north of I-90 \nthis afternoon. On Tuesday there will be zonal (west to east) flow \nover North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This will \nallow warm temperatures to remain with dry weather. On Tuesday there \nwill be strong low-level and mid-level winds. This will bring windy \nconditions to North-central Montana with the strongest winds along \nthe Rocky Mountain Front. On Tuesday there will be light rain and \nsnow showers over the northern Rocky Mountain Front.\n\nOn Wednesday and Thursday zonal flow remains over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana with strong low-level and mid-\nlevel winds. This will bring warm and mostly dry weather to the area \nwith breezy conditons across North-central Montana on Wednesday \nand Thursday. On Friday an upper-level ridge builds briefly in \nover North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This will \nallow temperatures to warm up with mostly dry weather across the \narea. Friday afternoon/evening an upper-level trough will briefly \nmove over North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. On \nSaturday and Sunday an upper-level ridge will build back in over \nNorth-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. After a cool \nday on Saturday due to the upper-level trough Friday evening \ntemperatures will rebound on Sunday. It will be mostly dry this \nweekend. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nThis afternoon there is a 20 - 35% chance for thunderstorms across \nsouthern Gallatin and Madison Counties. This afternoon there is a\n40 - 70% chance for a tenth of an inch of rain or greater in the \nWest Yellowstone area. On Tuesday across the Northern Rocky \nMountain Front there is a 60 - 80% chance for wind gusts of 75 mph\nor greater. On Tuesday across the plains west of I-15 there is a \n40 - 70% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph or greater. As a result a\nHigh Wind Warning was issued for the northern Rocky Mountain \nFront and plains west of I-15 from 12 AM Tuesday to noon on \nTuesday. -IG",
